<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Nova generated environment; SDFormat 1.12; SI metres/kg/radians; right-handed Z-up. Static geometry is baked into the nova_environment model frame. Each movable object is its own non-static model posed at its body origin: inertial link (mass, COM, diagonal inertia about COM), convex contact, and for doors/drawers a passive revolute/prismatic joint to world with limits, damping and friction. Free props have no joint. No robot dynamics or plugins synthesized. Gravity/contact coefficients come from scene source plus optional user overrides. World timestep is an explicit 0.002 second default. Runtime physics untested. -->
